    "result": "I've analyzed the invoicing/parsing.py file and created a comprehensive NOTES.md file that explains how the invoice text parser works. Here's what I've documented:\n\n## Input Format\nThe parser expects plain-text invoices with a specific structure containing header fields like Invoice, Customer, Issued, Terms, and Discount, followed by line items in a pipe-separated format.\n\n## Functions and Their Purpose\nI've outlined each function in the parser:\n- `split_headers()` - separates headers from item lines\n- Individual parsing functions for each header field (number, customer, issued, terms, discount)\n- `parse_item()` - handles line item parsing with validation\n- `parse_invoice_text()` - the main orchestrator that calls all the parsers\n\n## Error Reporting\nThe parser uses a custom `ParseError` exception that provides descriptive messages including line numbers and clear explanations of what went wrong during parsing.\n\nThe NOTES.md file provides a complete reference for understanding how this invoice parser works without modifying any of the existing code.",
